OL,3,AThe start-ups hoping to return battery
OL,4,Amaking to the US
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs heatwaves scorched Europe this
OL,7,Fsummer, workers at a US battery company
OL,8,Fnoticed an uptick in demand.
OL,10,FSan Diego-based Unigrid sells a nine
OL,11,Fkilowatt hour battery for people's
OL,12,Fhomes. Sweltering European homeowners
OL,13,Fwere apparently looking for ways of
OL,14,Fstoring power when it was available
OL,15,Ffrom the grid at lower rates. They
OL,16,Fcould then run air conditioners more
OL,17,Fcheaply, off the battery, during the
OL,18,Fworst heat of the day.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
